  "choresDeleteDialogBody": "This removes '{choreTitle}' from your list. You can't view it again yet.",
  "@choresDeleteDialogBody": {
    "description": "Body of the chore delete-confirmation dialog. Deliberately states only what the user can verify (the chore leaves every list) -- it used to claim 'its history is kept', which is true in the DB but unobservable: every read path filters deletedAt IS NULL and no history screen exists, so the claim invited a destructive tap on a safety net that didn't exist (triage.md T1.2/D2). Not worded as permanent either, since the data genuinely is retained. TODO(F19): once the chore history view ships, restore stronger copy that also states history is kept and viewable -- see triage.md D2's two-step ordering.",
    "placeholders": {
      "choreTitle": {
        "type": "String",
        "example": "Wash dishes"
      }
    }
  },

